2a86462a1ab20c68151719ba4635e3c294391e64:docs/security/PQ_CELL_DEADLINE_NATIVE_CRYPTO_V1.md:102:- The loopback swarm fixture is not a WAN/DHT or multi-operator acceptance
2a86462a1ab20c68151719ba4635e3c294391e64:docs/security/PQ_CELL_SWARM_LOOPBACK_RESEARCH_V1.md:12:PCS1 connects several **real OS peer processes** on literal 127.0.0.1 through bounded TCP framing. The server is explicitly loopback-only and uses ephemeral test-key files. Requests contain BE32(217) plus the exact inherited 217-byte PCQ1 challenge. Replies contain BE32(n) plus the inherited signed PCR1 response, with a strict maximum of 12 + 1MiB + 1 + 12*48 + 3487 bytes. Oversize length is rejected before payload allocation. This is **not** an authenticated public P2P transport.
